WEBVTT

00:09:26.989 --> 00:09:31.836
And so art as organizing is not
just concerned with artists' intentions,

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:33.866
but their actual impact.

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:36.122
Great art is not a monologue.

00:09:36.146 --> 00:09:39.935
Great art is a dialogue
between the artist and the people.

00:09:41.454 --> 00:09:44.229
PA: Four years ago, this artist ...

00:09:44.253 --> 00:09:46.486
AM: and this organizer ...

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:48.995
PA: found that we were not just a match.

00:09:49.019 --> 00:09:50.414
AM: We were a mirror.

00:09:50.438 --> 00:09:53.351
PA: Our worlds truly did collide,

00:09:53.375 --> 00:09:54.604
and in many ways ...

00:09:54.628 --> 00:09:55.919
AM: they combined.

00:09:56.367 --> 00:09:58.232
PA: We learned so much about movement,

00:09:58.256 --> 00:10:01.773
about love and about art
at its most impactful: